  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>a5c74bd62993e462c6a9a88bdc0e5c30</srcmd5>
    <version>0.11.0</version>
    <time>1771605999</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>- Update to version 0.11.0:
  * svt-av1: Support crf quarter steps:
    + defaults to -crf-increment to 0.25 if svt-av1 &gt;= 4.0.0
  * svt-av1: Widen default crf search range [10, 55] -&gt; [5, 70]
  * Use ffmpeg `-fps_mode passthrough` for all sample encodes.
    This improves VMAF scores in some cases.
  * Use explicit pixel format in xpsnr calls, use highest quality
    format of the ref &amp; distorted streams.
    This can improve scores in some cases.
  * Wait for vmaf/xpsnr processes to finish e.g. to allow custom
    logging to flush.
  * Update sample-encode json output to use float `predicted_encode_seconds`.
  * Fix higher crf-search VMAF tolerance than expected when using
    `--crf-increment` values above 1.</comment>
    <requestid>1334186</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>3ce9c404a3f1d7e09332f820c2c2448d</srcmd5>
    <version>0.11.7</version>
    <time>1792344188</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>- Update to version 0.11.7:
  * New encode and auto-encode --verify/--fail-fast options (plus
    --verify-decode and --verify-duration) to catch damaged or cut
    results and input decode errors
  * crf-search --stdout-format json; sample-encode json output gains
    type, crf and from_cache keys
  * Encode to a temporary file, then atomically rename to the
    destination; fix auto-encode --keep
  * Sample-encode can compute XPSNR and VMAF together
    (--xpsnr --and-vmaf); new --xpsnr-pix-format option
  * svt-av1: quarter crf steps by default, wider crf search range,
    version detection via ffmpeg
  * libx265: default --enc tag:v=hvc1 for better compatibility
  * Correct License tag to MIT AND MPL-2.0 (vendored option-ext,
    pulled in via dirs-sys, is MPL-2.0 and linked into the binary)
  * CVE-2025-55159 (boo#1248057): vendored slab is 0.4.12, above
    the 0.4.11 fix</comment>
    <requestid>1385687</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
